              {
                "id": "aehnrb9gi1u2r2y",
                "text": "Free Energy: Summary"
              }
            ],
            "id": "pyhgl7g68646sfn",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Gibbs free energy ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": ") is a state function defined with regard to system quantities only and may be used to predict the spontaneity of a process. A negative value for ΔG indicates a spontaneous process; a positive ΔG indicates a nonspontaneous process; and a ΔG of zero indicates that the system is at equilibrium. A number of approaches to the computation of free energy changes are possible."
              }
            ],
            "id": "m9wobpdmxgpztdg",
            "type": "p"
          },
